                <p style={{ color: '#64748b' }}>Frequency check: an equipment's Yes/No frequency columns (daily, mid-week, weekly, monthly, quarterly, annual) set its medallion. A frequency is within its window when a clean of at least that kind (a weekly log counts for daily and mid-week, a monthly log for everything, a log with no kind set for everything) is dated within 1 / 7 / 7 / 31 / 92 / 366 days of today, overdue when none is and every month of that window has been read for the equipment, and not read yet otherwise.</p>
                <p style={{ color: '#64748b' }}>Room and area rows use the done-or-blank method: a check on every day on which any of their equipment was cleaned, and a bar counting the equipment cleaned on at least one day on screen, missed (every month on screen read, no log) or not read yet. Paperwork: a marker with a paper clip has a picture or file attached (the log's {LOG_FILE_COLUMN} column); a click reads it from Dataverse and shows it with a Download button.</p>
                <p style={{ color: '#64748b' }}>Completion percentages (full mode: click the CJ Schwan's logo on the MSS tab; the plain MSS shows none of them and reads no production plan): every frequency letter on an equipment is one job per period (D per day, MW and W per Monday-to-Sunday week, M per month, Q per quarter, A per year). A job is done when a clean of at least that kind (same ranks as the medallion) is dated inside its period, missed when every month it touches has been read for the equipment and there is none, and left out while a month is unread. The day rows show the Daily jobs of that day (done % and number not done); the Sunday rows every daily, mid-week and weekly job of that week (the monthly, quarterly and annual jobs appear only in the figures above the grid and under the room and area names, as not done / due, counted over the months on screen). With the production plan read, equipment in an area a line follows (Line Downtime tab) has a Daily job only on a day that line had an hour or more without production, one Daily job for a weekend it was down (shown on the Sunday, done by a clean on either day), and its mid-week and weekly jobs only in a week the line ran (an hour of production or more); a week no plan row reaches is left out. All other equipment keeps a Daily job every day and a weekly job every week. The two top figures count the jobs whose period ended inside the months on screen, and since 1 January (a period still running counts only once done). A figure in italics is for a day or week not over yet, a dotted one leaves out jobs of equipment not read yet. 90% and above is green, 70% and above yellow, below red (PCT_GOOD and PCT_WARN at the top of the file); DAILY_ON lists the weekdays on which a Daily job falls due. They follow the search filter. Only equipment with a cleaning frequency has jobs (the room and area bars, Load all and Equipment loaded count every equipment). They cover only the months read from the log so far: a month not read yet is left out, not counted as missed, and a job that reaches into a month not read yet (a quarterly or annual job, the first week of the year or of the months on screen) counts only once it is done. Read year to date also reads the December before the year, where the first week of the year starts.</p>
                <p style={{ color: '#64748b' }}>Logs load per visible equipment and month, never the whole table: a log is shown on the equipment whose id is stored in its craa5_equipmentguid. Old entries whose id is blank or matches no equipment are matched by equipment name (amber). Nothing loads until an area is expanded on the Compliance Matrix tab.</p>
